# WISC reference boards (read-only)

Everything under **`docs/reference/wisc-board/`** is **legacy production reference** for current WanOS on WISC hardware. It is **not** the wanos-pcb-v1 design tree.

## Hard rule

**Do not edit** any KiCad sources under `docs/reference/wisc-board/`, including:

- KiCad sources (`.kicad_pro`, `.kicad_sch`, `.kicad_pcb`, `.kicad_prl`, lib tables)
- Custom libraries (`*.kicad_sym`, `*.pretty/`, footprints)
- Fabrication exports (`gerbers/`, drills, zips, BOM xlsx) except via `_donotcommit/` archive policy
- KiCad lock/history sidecars (`.lck`, `.history/`)

This applies even when the operator has a WISC board **open in KiCad** or asks to "fix" something on reference material.

## Allowed

- **Read** schematics, PCB, gerbers, and libraries for analysis
- **Konnect / file reads** against these paths (e.g. `get_project_info`, `open_project`, `get_board_info` with `source: file`)
- **Document** findings in product docs (`docs/*.md` outside `reference/wisc-board/`) or pipeline docs (`docs/todo/`)
- **Copy patterns** into `projects/wanos-board/` only after an explicit **`implement`** / **`ship`** / **`patch`** command on wanos-pcb-v1 work — and only when locked in wanos product docs, not because WISC does it that way ([`wanos-greenfield-wisc-intent.mdc`](wanos-greenfield-wisc-intent.mdc))

## Where new design lives

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `docs/reference/wisc-board/` | **Reference only** — summaries + read-only KiCad |
| `projects/wanos-board/` | **wanos-pcb-v1** KiCad project (when S1 starts) |
| `docs/board-spec.md`, `docs/field-wiring.md`, … | Canonical target spec for the new board |

## If reference must change

Stop and ask the operator. Archive or fork outside this tree, or confirm a deliberate exception — do not silently patch reference KiCad files.
